            <ArticleTitle>Intraamniotic Infection and the Term Neonate.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>385-387</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1891/0730-0832.36.6.385</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Intraamniotic infection (IAI) may occur when the amniotic membranes are ruptured &gt;18 hours prior to birth. The term neonate is at risk for early onset sepsis. This article describes the pathophysiology of IAI and the role of the mother-baby nurse during the anticipated birth and the ongoing assessment of the neonate.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
